{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/sources"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(toIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parentEdge(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/path(to:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestPathTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Distance"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ties.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The first relaxation to a vertex’s final distance wins. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortest-path predecessor of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" settled first. Vertices at equal distance settle in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unspecified order, so when several vertices at the same smallest distance lead to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" along"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortest paths, which one is the parent is unspecified. Among parallel edges from the parent,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent edge is the cheapest, and the first in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order among equals."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree holds a copy of the graph, so looking a vertex up never hashes on a representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with cheap vertex indices. While the tree is alive, the next mutation of the original copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it; a tree of a graph about to change should be read and dropped first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Several sources."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Each source starts at distance zero ("},{"code":".one","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over a semiring) with no parent. Dijkstra’s algorithm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and breadth-first search never improve on that, so a source keeps no parent even when another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"source reaches it. Bellman–Ford treats the sources as one super-source (NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"_bellman_ford","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): a negative path from one source to another improves the second, which then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has that distance, a parent and a path from the first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Semirings.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Over a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SelectiveSemiring"},{"text":" a distance is the ⊗-product of a path’s weights, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"best by the natural order ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"text":", and a vertex is reached exactly when its distance is not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zero"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": two correct trees can choose different parents on ties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Shortest paths from one or more sources: for each reached vertex, its distance, its parent and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the edge from the parent (a forest when there are several sources, LEMON’s “shortest path tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(forest)”)."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestPathTree"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree.swift#L29","fileName":"ShortestPathTree.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"ShortestPathTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/sources":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sources","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/sources","type":"topic","title":"sources","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sources, in the order given, each once."}],"url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree\/sources"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/path(to:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree\/path(to:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/path(to:)","kind":"symbol","title":"path(to:)","abstract":[{"text":"A shortest path from a source to ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", both included, with the edges it takes (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tell parallel edges apart): the trivial path ","type":"text"},{"code":"[vertex]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a source, ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"